rem kmp.pnx - basic bench `kmp`: Knuth-Morris-Pratt over a text of four letters from a linear generator
rem (a b a c: the code is a=0, b=1, c=2), the pattern a a c b c a, the hits counted. pnx kmp.pnx N (default 4000000).
use io .
use env .
use str .
const most 4000000
array txt int most
array pat int 6
array pf int 6
array letters int 4
def main or fail do
  1 env.arg or_else to e "4000000" end str.to_int or_fail to n
  0 0 set letters  1 1 set letters  0 2 set letters  2 3 set letters
  0 n range do to i
    i 1103515245 mul 12345 add 16 shr 3 bit_and letters idx i set txt
  end each
  0 0 set pat  0 1 set pat  2 2 set pat  1 3 set pat  2 4 set pat  0 5 set pat
  6 to m
  0 0 set pf
  0 to k
  1 to q
  loop
    q m lt not if break . end
    loop
      k 0 gt not if break . end
      k pat idx  q pat idx ne not if break . end
      k 1 sub pf idx to k
    end
    k pat idx  q pat idx eq if k 1 add to k end
    k q set pf
    q 1 add to q
  end
  0 to state
  0 to hits
  0 n range do to i
    loop
      state 0 gt not if break . end
      state pat idx  i txt idx ne not if break . end
      state 1 sub pf idx to state
    end
    state pat idx  i txt idx eq if state 1 add to state end
    state m eq if hits 1 add to hits  state 1 sub pf idx to state end
  end each
  args "kmp " n " " hits . cat io.println
end
main or_else to e args "kmp: " e err_text . cat io.println end
